\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The upright measure}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The integration measure uses the upright #{\extd}, the same mark as
the exterior derivative. Mathematical physics writes #{dx} or #{d\mu}
in italic, and geometric calculus writes a directed measure
#{\extd^{n}x}. The integral sign is what marks the measure. A linear
change of reference volume is otherwise the same statement.}
